+ * The input is not changed. Any NaN item gives NaN, since NaN cannot be put in order.
+ * @param {number[]} xs
+ * @param {number} p from 0 to 100, both included
+ * @returns {number} e.g. percentile([1, 2, 3, 4, 5], 25) gives 2 and percentile([1, 2, 3, 4], 25) gives 1.75; NaN for an empty array
+ * @throws {TypeError} if xs is not an array, or any item or p is not a number
+ * @throws {RangeError} if p is NaN or outside 0 to 100
+ */
