+ * The greatest common divisor of two integers: the largest whole number that divides both. The sign of the
+ * inputs does not matter, so the result is never negative. gcd(a, 0) is the absolute value of a, and gcd(0, 0) is 0.
+ * Works for any integers a number can hold, including those above Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER.
+ * @param {number} a
+ * @param {number} b
+ * @returns {number} e.g. gcd(12, 18) gives 6, gcd(-12, 18) gives 6 and gcd(5, 0) gives 5
+ * @throws {TypeError} if a or b is not a number
+ * @throws {RangeError} if a or b is not an integer (this includes NaN and Infinity)
